What the file says about itself:
  The owner's P900 photo DSCN7496 (28 March 2026, 17:34), levelled on its sea horizon (already rotated by
  roll), contrast corrected, w x h px. Scale s (px/rad) from the EXIF focal length, the same for every model.
  Placed ON THE HORIZON: photo row `horizon` = the model's sea top, in every state c (apparent curvature).
  az: azimuth of the photo centre (rad, relative to BORD_SITE.az), the only free parameter, one for all models
  (a direction does not depend on the shape): that of the best-matching state. states[]: each model's OWN best
  azimuth and its match of the buildings (score = correlation; steel-man for the plane). meas: named roofs above the photo's
  sea line (px at full resolution, mrad, m at their distance) and the curvature c / refraction k they imply.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/other.json: edit that, not this file.
